cerberus-signer for Debian
==========================

The service is installed but NOT enabled or started. The Enclave Image File is
NOT shipped by default: it bakes in the KMS-encrypted CA private key
(per-deployment). Build it and copy it in:

    make eif-<arch>                                  # ssh-cert-signer-<arch>.eif
    sudo cp ssh-cert-signer-<arch>.eif /usr/share/cerberus/ssh-cert-signer.eif

(Or install the opt-in cerberus-signer-eif package, which places it there.)
Review /etc/default/cerberus-signer (ENCLAVE_CID/CPU/MEMORY), then:

    systemctl enable --now cerberus-signer

Requires aws-nitro-enclaves-cli (nitro-cli) and a Nitro-enabled EC2 host.

 -- Paul Kilar <pkilar@gmail.com>
